      "sourceField": "monitor",
      "sourceExcerpt": "• Check potassium and renal function. • Escalate significant hyperkalemia or worsening renal function before routine administration. • Watch hypotension, dizziness and dehydration with other diuretics/RAAS blockers. • Do not casually add potassium supplements or potassium-containing salt substitutes. • After starting or changing the dose, arrange early potassium monitoring within one week under the prescribing plan, with closer monitoring when renal function or interacting drugs increase risk.",
